    "lawCode": "Amd §3602, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6400\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the education law, in relation to\nthe computation of certain building aid\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would authorize two multi-year cost allowances in a\nfive-year period for the computation of Building Aid for Yonkers\nPublic School projects authorized pursuant to chapter 355 of the laws\nof 2016. Additional multi-year cost allowances could not be reset for\neffected buildings for a period of ten-years after establishment of\nthe first maximum cost allowance.\n\nIn addition, the bill would allow the Yonkers Public Schools to\nreceive an enhanced building aid ratio for projects authorized\npursuant to chapter 355 of the laws of 2016.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one of the bill amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 6 of\nsection 3602 of the education law by adding a new subparagraph 7 to\nsuch paragraph (a) to provide that projects authorized pursuant to\nchapter three hundred fifty-five of the laws of two thousand sixteen\nshall be permitted to utilize two multi-year cost allowances in a\nfive-year period. The new subparagraph 7 also provides that subsequent\nmulti-year cost allowances may not be established for a period of\nten-years from the date of the first multi-year cost allowance\nauthorized by this subparagraph.\n\nSection two of the bill amends subparagraph 2 of paragraph c of\nsubdivision 6 of section 3602 of education law by adding a new clause\n(d) which will allow that for school years 2017-2018 and thereafter,\nschool building projects authorized pursuant to chapter three hundred\nfifty-five of the laws of two thousand sixteen shall compute aid using\na building aid ratio of ninety-eight hundredths.\n\nSection three of the bill states that the act shall take effect\nimmediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nNew York State recognized the critical needs of Yonkers public school\nbuildings when they enacted Chapter 355 of the laws of 2016, which\nestablished Phase I of the Yonkers City School District Joint Schools\nConstruction and Modernization Act. The Yonkers School District is in\ndesperate need of additional classroom seats, replacement of old and\noutdated school buildings and remediation to address health and safety\nissues. The expansive amount of school facility needs cannot be\nundertaken by the Yonkers School District without additional support\nfrom the State. This bill is intended to ensure the District can move\nforward with Phase I.\n\nThe State utilizes multi-year cost allowances when calculating\nBuilding Aid for eligible capital projects. Once a school district has\nreached its maximum cost allowance (MCA) for a particular project,\nadditional State contribution is not available for a period of\nfive-years. This particular limitation will have an adverse impact on\nthe efficient execution of the Yonkers projects, increase the cost of\nthese projects, restrict the use of limited resources and\nunnecessarily disrupt the academic process. This bill would address\nthe problem by providing two multi-year cost allowances in a ten-year\nperiod.\n\nThis bill also recognizes the pressing facility needs for the District\nby providing Yonkers with an enhanced building aid ratio for projects\nauthorized pursuant to Phase I of the Joint Schools Construction and\nModernization Act.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThis measure will reduce costs for the Yonkers Public Schools and the\ncost to the State is to be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
