    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6400A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the education law, in relation to\nthe computation of certain building aid\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would authorize two multi-year cost allowances in a\nfive-year period for the computation of Building Aid for three new\nYonkers school construction projects authorized pursuant to chapter\n355 of the laws of 2016. Additional multi-year cost allowances could\nnot be reset for effected buildings for a period of ten-years after\nestablishment of the first maximum cost allowance.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one of the bill amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 6 of\nsection 3602 of the education law by adding a new subparagraph 7 to\nsuch paragraph (a) to provide that for three new construction projects\nauthorized pursuant to chapter three hundred fifty-five of the laws of\ntwo thousand sixteen shall be permitted to utilize two multi-year cost\nallowances in a five-year period. The new subparagraph 7 also provides\nthat subsequent multi-year cost allowances may not be established for\na period of ten-years from the date of the first multi-year cost\nallowance authorized by this subparagraph. Section two of the bill\nstates that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nNew York State recognized the critical needs of Yonkers public school\nbuildings when they enacted Chapter 355 of the laws of 2016, which\nestablished Phase I of the Yonkers City School District Joint Schools\nConstruction and Modernization Act. The Yonkers School District is in\ndesperate need of additional classroom seats, replacement of old and\noutdated school buildings and remediation to address health and safety\nissues. The expansive amount of school facility needs cannot be under-\ntaken by the Yonkers School District without additional support from\nthe State. This bill is intended to ensure the District can move\nforward with Phase I.The State utilizes multi-year cost allowances\nwhen calculating Building Aid for eligible capital projects. Once a\nschool district has reached its maximum cost allowance (MCA) for a\nparticular project, additional State contribution is not available for\na period of five-years. This particular limitation will have an\nadverse impact on the efficient execution of the Yonkers projects,\nincrease the cost of these projects, restrict the use of limited\nresources and unnecessarily disrupt the academic process. This bill\nwould address the problem by providing two multi-year cost allowances\nin a ten-year period.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThis measure will reduce costs for the Yonkers Public Schools and the\ncost to the State is to be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
